        "calls": 1,
        "title": "Invalid skills refusal names the rejected skill and field",
        "summary": "Adds `invalidSkillsRefusal` to `common/src/desktop-cloud/project-settings.ts`, replacing the previous generic 400 response for rejected cloud skill payloads with a specific message identifying the offending skill, field, and Zod error code. The implementation handles Zod v4 union failures by selecting the branch with the fewest issues, ensuring encoding errors in base64 uploads are not misattributed to missing fields in the plain upload variant. To prevent leaking user-authored content, the function only quotes the skill name if it matches the new `SKILL_NAME_PATTERN` regex, which was extracted from the schema to verify the name is safe to echo.",
        "significance": "notable",
        "audience": "end-users",
        "evidence": "The diff in `common/src/desktop-cloud/project-settings.ts` adds the exported function `invalidSkillsRefusal` and supporting private helpers (`reportableIssue`, `closestBranchIssue`, `renderIssuePath`, `skillNameAt`), and extracts the skill name regex into the new export `SKILL_NAME_PATTERN`.",
        "userVisible": true,
        "confidence": "medium",
